  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">COVID-19: Fiscal Resilience and Social Protection Support Program (Subprogram 1)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed Program is part of a comprehensive and integrated package of support from the Asian Development Bank (ADB) to the Government of Georgia to help address adverse health, social and economic impacts of the coronavirus disease (COVID-19) pandemic. The Program supports Georgia&apos;s return to inclusive economic growth by addressing longstanding institutional fragilities that were further exposed as a result of the COVID-19 crisis. The Program is aligned with ADB&apos;s Strategy 2030, including operational priorities on addressing remaining poverty and reducing inequalities, accelerating progress in gender equality, strengthening governance and institutional capacity. The Program is also aligned with the ADB Country Partnership Strategy, 20182022 for Georgia.</narrative>
  </description>
